Hi,

currently aroma.affymetrix only recognizes so called "dChip genome
information" files.  On the dChip website
[http://www.dchip.org/gene_info_file.htm] you will find such files for
some of the Affymetrix chips.  I know they have them for all the SNP
arrays, but I'm not sure about the exon arrays.  On the above page,
there are information how to create such files youself from Affymetrix
CSV annotation files.  Creating genome information files is unexplored
land for me.  I've also got a brief section on genome information
files under the Section "For Developers" on the group page.

Implementation details: If you already have an annotation file for
your exon chip type in another file format, you could create a new
class inheriting from the GenomeInformation class, and then implement
the static method fromChipType(chipType).  This is what the
DChipGenomeInformation class does, e.g.

  DChipGenomeInformation$fromChipType(chipType)

A static method is nothing but a regular S3 method with first argument
named 'static', e.g. fromChipType.DChipGenomeInformation(static, ...).
 Some time ago I played around with such a class for Affymetrix CSV
files, but since they are very large and in a complex ASCII format
they are really slow to read, and since the dChip genome files were
available I used them instead.  Ideally Affymetrix comes up with a
binary format for this.

Hope this helps

Henrik

